1
00:02:04,210 --> 00:02:07,530
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE
FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:07,595 --> 00:02:30,175
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:14,650
What are you waiting for? Take him away!

4
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:35,000
Know your place.

5
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:36,420
We caught Osman, your highness.

6
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:38,440
As you ordered, they are taking him here.

7
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:49,140
Today is the Day of Titans!

8
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:52,080
Day of Titans!

9
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:23,580
Welcome to Hell, Osman.

10
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:26,720
Are you the Hellhound?

11
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:32,640
Soon, you will understand whether it is
Hellhound or Azreal.

12
00:08:34,559 --> 00:08:35,760
So be it.

13
00:08:39,539 --> 00:08:42,179
Allah is eternal! Allah is the truth!

14
00:08:47,780 --> 00:08:50,040
Take Osman inside! Hurry up!

15
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:51,480
Close the gates at once!

16
00:09:20,620 --> 00:09:22,380
With Osman, came three other Turks.

17
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,800
Flatyos is taking care of them, your
highness.

18
00:09:24,860 --> 00:09:25,900
Osman…

19
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:11,520
Hurry up!

20
00:10:12,180 --> 00:10:13,980
Break down the door!

21
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:16,320
You shouldn’t come to this castle this
often.

22
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:22,280
Sometimes I wonder if you’ve become the
victim of your anger.

23
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:27,580
I will come here frequently until you
empty this castle.

24
00:10:28,340 --> 00:10:30,100
Frequently, huh?

25
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:39,320
Still hopeful, you are!

26
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:44,800
Be quick!

27
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:49,720
Hurry up!

28
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:56,160
Osman, I don’t know if you’ve noticed but
you are going to do die very soon.

29
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:00,460
We were taught to live like this, Nikola.

30
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:04,440
As if we are always going to die soon.

31
00:11:08,020 --> 00:11:10,320
As if you are going to die very soon, huh?

32
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:14,980
I learned so many thing about Turks.

33
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:18,060
However, if I combine all of them…

34
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:22,840
… they would only make a very short book.

35
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:28,600
A short book is enough for a decent man.

36
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,540
We are told to read!

37
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:37,680
For this reason, even our arrows have only
a single target.

38
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:44,960
Our Dhikr is one as well as our object.

39
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:48,200
This is what makes us invincible!

40
00:11:48,860 --> 00:11:51,800
But you lost, Osman!

41
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:55,760
Those who think of Death as Shahada never
loses!

42
00:11:56,740 --> 00:12:00,280
Our path is Victory, and our name is
Victor!

43
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:04,280
But you lost, Osman! You lost!

44
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:10,700
Did you really think you’d win like this?

45
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,740
Did you really? You lost!

46
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:21,220
This is it!

47
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:39,100
Find them!

48
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:41,400
Don’t let them leave the castle!

49
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:52,060
Osman is fleeing!

50
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:56,600
What’s happening? Nikola!

51
00:12:56,900 --> 00:12:59,940
They are fighting inside! Osman must have
broken free!

52
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:00,800
Nikola!

53
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:02,260
Nikola!

54
00:13:29,860 --> 00:13:30,760
Nikola!

55
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,060
Break down the gate!

56
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:39,150
Nikola!

57
00:13:58,780 --> 00:14:00,220
Break down the gate!

58
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:02,560
Nikola!

59
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:10,180
Break down the gate!

60
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,340
Break down the gate!

61
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:24,660
Catch him!

62
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:28,200
Nikola!

63
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:33,380
Nikola, are you okay?

64
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:40,520
Nikola!

65
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:43,200
Damn it, it won’t open!

66
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:46,200
I’m going to kill you, Osman!

67
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:47,660
Don’t leave him alone!

68
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,180
Osman!

69
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:11,000
It doesn’t work.

70
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:32,340
Osman!

71
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:03,500
You can’t run away forever, Osman!

72
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:29,380
Let’s go!

73
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:49,880
Open the gate, Aygül!

74
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:41,560
Osman!

75
00:18:43,020 --> 00:18:43,880
My Bey!

76
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:46,400
Aygül!

77
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,100
Get out!

78
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:53,280
Go!

79
00:19:04,620 --> 00:19:05,560
Come on!

80
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:07,680
Come on, Osman!

81
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:16,580
Osman!

82
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:18,480
We are leaving, brothers!

83
00:19:28,060 --> 00:19:29,600
Let’s go!

84
00:19:46,980 --> 00:19:50,060
We are going to save the prisoners
in exchange of golds.

85
00:19:59,020 --> 00:20:03,540
I will come back. Place a hay cart at the
marked area.

86
00:20:14,340 --> 00:20:15,420
Osman!

87
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:31,600
One day, these games are going to be over!

88
00:20:31,740 --> 00:20:33,780
We will have a fight against each other!

89
00:20:33,860 --> 00:20:36,180
Lion Hunter Flatyos and Kara Osman!

90
00:20:36,820 --> 00:20:38,420
On that day…

91
00:20:38,460 --> 00:20:40,180
… I promise you that…

92
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:43,200
… I’m going to eat your heart out!

93
00:20:44,940 --> 00:20:47,540
Open the gate!

94
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:01,380
Let’s go!

95
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:43,900
Feudal Landlord Nikola is dying!

96
00:21:43,980 --> 00:21:45,580
How can he die?

97
00:21:46,700 --> 00:21:48,720
Hurry up!

98
00:22:01,060 --> 00:22:01,920
Nikola!

99
00:23:06,140 --> 00:23:09,160
You said Romans would be strong once
again.

100
00:23:15,500 --> 00:23:18,720
You said we’d take our flag to Jerusalem.

101
00:23:19,460 --> 00:23:20,300
Nikola...

102
00:23:22,120 --> 00:23:23,360
Hear me out Nikola!

103
00:23:23,760 --> 00:23:24,820
Hear me.

104
00:23:48,580 --> 00:23:51,140
Who is going to resurrect you now Rome!?

105
00:25:24,800 --> 00:25:28,280
They stabbed our lands just like this
dagger, Nikola.

106
00:25:36,320 --> 00:25:37,780
But I promise you...

107
00:25:41,420 --> 00:25:46,280
...that I will pull them out just like I
pull this dagger.

108
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:51,300
Nikola?!

109
00:25:52,440 --> 00:25:56,900
Nikola!

110
00:25:57,740 --> 00:25:59,500
Soldier, summon the physician!

111
00:26:00,120 --> 00:26:02,200
Nikola!

112
00:26:02,440 --> 00:26:04,800
Hold on my friend!

113
00:26:09,100 --> 00:26:13,660
Nikola?!

114
00:26:39,280 --> 00:26:40,760
Go!

115
00:27:06,540 --> 00:27:08,100
Allah is eternal!

116
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:12,460
It’s a trap!

117
00:27:13,400 --> 00:27:14,960
Allah is the truth!

118
00:28:01,780 --> 00:28:03,320
What were you doing there?

119
00:28:11,900 --> 00:28:13,420
Did we kill him?

120
00:28:23,100 --> 00:28:24,960
The dagger didn’t go down deep.

121
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:34,060
I told you not to come.

122
00:28:35,200 --> 00:28:39,620
I want to unsheathe my sword and die for
our cause.

123
00:29:04,380 --> 00:29:05,600
Catch that one!

124
00:29:08,500 --> 00:29:10,900
It’s me, Osman!

125
00:29:14,100 --> 00:29:15,560
Aygül?

126
00:29:17,080 --> 00:29:19,080
What are you doing here?

127
00:29:19,880 --> 00:29:21,520
I’ve come to help you.

128
00:29:23,080 --> 00:29:25,760
We don’t need your help! Go back at once!

129
00:29:26,100 --> 00:29:28,140
Are you afraid that I will die?

130
00:29:30,020 --> 00:29:32,700
If so, don’t. Because I’m already dead.

131
00:29:33,520 --> 00:29:35,900
I’m a spirit which came to help you.

132
00:29:40,900 --> 00:29:42,800
I won’t leave even if you tell me to.

133
00:29:43,660 --> 00:29:47,120
Aygül, may you do what I tell you to!
Don’t follow me!

134
00:29:47,340 --> 00:29:48,980
I want to help you!

135
00:29:49,020 --> 00:29:50,980
Then, do what I ask you to!

136
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:54,540
Don’t follow me, Aygül!

137
00:29:57,120 --> 00:29:58,880
The order is yours, my Bey!

138
00:30:04,380 --> 00:30:05,560
Let’s go!

139
00:30:13,100 --> 00:30:15,480
Your eyes killed me, Osman!

140
00:30:16,860 --> 00:30:18,840
What can our enemy do to me?

141
00:30:20,280 --> 00:30:22,760
I grew up waiting for you to come!

142
00:30:23,500 --> 00:30:26,800
You can’t prevent me from dying for
your path!

143
00:30:38,380 --> 00:30:42,140
I told you not to come but you did
anyways.

144
00:30:43,280 --> 00:30:44,400
Yes, It’s true.

145
00:30:44,440 --> 00:30:45,920
Then, why did you come?

146
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:49,240
Don’t question but see me, Osman.

147
00:30:50,720 --> 00:30:52,940
I’m nothing like old Aygül anymore.

148
00:30:53,580 --> 00:30:55,440
I want to become an Alp.

149
00:30:57,160 --> 00:31:01,020
I want to become a martyr and reach to
heaven.

150
00:31:21,420 --> 00:31:22,340
Göktuğ.

151
00:31:25,040 --> 00:31:26,780
May you build a fire there.

152
00:31:28,940 --> 00:31:31,380
I will stigmatize the wound of uncle’s
daughter.

153
00:31:49,960 --> 00:31:51,500
Come with me, my girl.

154
00:32:27,740 --> 00:32:29,120
My beautiful Bala.

155
00:32:37,700 --> 00:32:40,360
You are sorrowful of not having a child.

156
00:32:42,220 --> 00:32:45,440
But Aygul feels the opposite.

157
00:32:46,920 --> 00:32:51,160
For this reasons, they say ‘the best in
something’.

158
00:32:56,120 --> 00:33:00,320
And Allah tells us to never lose our hope.

159
00:33:17,180 --> 00:33:21,440
With hope, we’ll go on our path.

160
00:33:29,560 --> 00:33:31,920
Do you love Osman Bey so much, Bala?

161
00:33:36,860 --> 00:33:38,600
How much do you love him?

162
00:33:48,260 --> 00:33:51,060
I don’t have to answer this
question, Targun.

163
00:33:53,240 --> 00:33:55,420
However, if you wonder this much…

164
00:33:59,380 --> 00:34:03,140
… I threw everything from my heart and
filled it with his love.

165
00:34:08,060 --> 00:34:13,980
If I loved a man this much, I’d rip out
everything from his heart besides myself.

166
00:34:37,460 --> 00:34:42,739
My Bala, do you think Osman vanquished
that dog already?

167
00:34:58,600 --> 00:35:01,900
The medallion and the map saved your
life, Nikola.

168
00:35:26,400 --> 00:35:31,600
Nikola, the new ruler of the new Rome.

169
00:35:37,560 --> 00:35:40,380
You want to become the emperor, huh?

170
00:35:46,640 --> 00:35:48,320
He did it, Flatyos.

171
00:35:51,580 --> 00:35:53,740
He entered the castle...

172
00:35:55,200 --> 00:35:57,240
... overcame the trap...

173
00:35:59,380 --> 00:36:01,140
…and killed me.

174
00:36:14,480 --> 00:36:17,040
Your dreams saved you, Nikola.

175
00:36:24,460 --> 00:36:26,700
The dreams of becoming the new Emperor.

176
00:36:37,620 --> 00:36:39,360
This is a sign.

177
00:36:41,500 --> 00:36:43,880
I am reborn, Flatyos.

178
00:36:45,620 --> 00:36:48,260
Just like Mithra who killed the black ox.

179
00:36:49,820 --> 00:36:52,920
Reborn, like the god of kings, Dionysus.

180
00:36:55,080 --> 00:36:57,560
Or, like Jesus Christ.

181
00:37:01,700 --> 00:37:04,120
I promise you that...

182
00:37:05,760 --> 00:37:07,520
... I’ll make them all pay for this.

183
00:37:09,320 --> 00:37:16,700
I’m going to wander around the Tents
of Kayıs, and impale them all.

184
00:37:18,420 --> 00:37:23,420
At the end, I’ll make a forest made out o
f impales.

185
00:37:44,900 --> 00:37:53,620
Then, I’ll place the head of Osman at the
top of those impales.

186
00:38:32,320 --> 00:38:34,820
Aygül!

187
00:38:36,200 --> 00:38:38,200
Let me do it, Aygül!

188
00:38:39,040 --> 00:38:43,580
It’s brand iron! What do you think you
are doing?

189
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:15,580
It’s brand and it hurts, uncle’s daughter.

190
00:39:22,260 --> 00:39:25,960
What’s the thing that hurts you more than
this brand iron, Aygül?

191
00:39:27,580 --> 00:39:29,240
Tell me what it is.

192
00:39:33,880 --> 00:39:36,840
I have a baby, Osman.

193
00:39:42,600 --> 00:39:44,060
What baby?

194
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:47,760
A baby, Osman.

195
00:39:51,480 --> 00:39:53,140
From Alişar.

196
00:39:58,580 --> 00:40:00,800
From the man who you beheaded.

197
00:40:03,220 --> 00:40:05,200
Choose your words wisely, Aygül.

198
00:40:07,860 --> 00:40:09,360
What Alişar?

199
00:40:11,420 --> 00:40:14,140
Every life given is from Allah.

200
00:40:29,780 --> 00:40:31,540
I have a nephew now, huh?

201
00:40:42,700 --> 00:40:44,320
Is it a boy?

202
00:40:48,840 --> 00:40:50,880
Tell me. Is it a boy?

203
00:41:01,040 --> 00:41:02,760
What’s his name?

204
00:41:04,220 --> 00:41:05,720
He doesn’t have one.

205
00:41:08,200 --> 00:41:09,780
Doesn’t have a name?

206
00:41:27,200 --> 00:41:29,380
Then, his uncle will name him!

207
00:41:44,920 --> 00:41:46,720
May his name be Kayıalp.

208
00:41:48,820 --> 00:41:50,520
May he be an Alp for Kayı.

209
00:41:55,660 --> 00:41:57,540
So, we have a new alp, my Bey.

210
00:41:59,480 --> 00:42:02,720
With Allah’s permission, he will be a
warrior like Aygül Hatun.

211
00:42:03,640 --> 00:42:04,880
Well said.

212
00:42:48,220 --> 00:42:50,160
What’s the meaning of this, Hazal?

213
00:42:51,340 --> 00:42:57,640
Dündar Bey. Do you want me to use this
sword?

214
00:43:01,380 --> 00:43:03,600
Against whom, you would use that sword?

215
00:43:07,420 --> 00:43:08,800
Against your daughter!

216
00:43:09,520 --> 00:43:15,420
What are you saying, Hatun? How will you
use that sword against my daughter?

217
00:43:16,760 --> 00:43:20,060
Like this! Just like she used it against
me!

218
00:43:24,760 --> 00:43:26,340
Where is Aygül?

219
00:43:26,760 --> 00:43:31,260
She was already at the Tent and Selcan
Hatun was hiding her from everyone!

220
00:43:33,840 --> 00:43:36,440
She set her against me as if she is an
Alp!

221
00:43:36,900 --> 00:43:38,740
She nearly killed me!

222
00:43:40,500 --> 00:43:43,980
Now I’m asking you, Dündar Bey!

223
00:43:46,180 --> 00:43:51,040
Am I to wait for the next time she is
going to attack me?

224
00:43:51,060 --> 00:43:54,820
Or am I to attack her with my sword?

225
00:43:56,760 --> 00:43:58,160
Where’s my daughter?

226
00:43:58,998 --> 00:44:00,163
Where?

227
00:44:01,111 --> 00:44:02,263
Where?

228
00:44:04,589 --> 00:44:06,685
May I enter, Dündar Bey?

229
00:44:14,572 --> 00:44:16,692
Come, Selcan Hatun.

230
00:45:23,691 --> 00:45:25,415
I'll come back later.

231
00:45:25,818 --> 00:45:27,725
Wait, Selcan Hatun.

232
00:45:33,736 --> 00:45:35,512
Whose baby is that?

233
00:45:42,297 --> 00:45:43,997
Your daughter's.

234
00:45:53,615 --> 00:45:54,700
Aygül's.

235
00:45:55,630 --> 00:45:57,101
You...

236
00:46:01,480 --> 00:46:03,057
What are you saying?

237
00:46:15,317 --> 00:46:16,541
Aygül's?

238
00:46:21,668 --> 00:46:23,116
How?

239
00:46:32,779 --> 00:46:38,900
From the man who was beheaded
by Osman. From Alişar.

240
00:46:54,127 --> 00:46:55,834
Alişar?

241
00:46:59,560 --> 00:47:01,093
Alişar...

242
00:47:05,101 --> 00:47:07,357
Why did you hide...

243
00:47:08,575 --> 00:47:10,623
...this baby from me...

244
00:47:11,386 --> 00:47:14,363
...all this time?

245
00:47:18,073 --> 00:47:19,392
Why?

246
00:48:27,421 --> 00:48:29,756
How can this man return alive?

247
00:48:37,507 --> 00:48:38,632
Aygül.

248
00:48:48,711 --> 00:48:49,772
My daughter...

249
00:49:10,171 --> 00:49:13,632
Your father is curious about where
you were, Aygül!

250
00:49:24,659 --> 00:49:28,185
We were at Kulucahisar, in the
lair of the enemy.

251
00:49:28,969 --> 00:49:32,674
We stabbed Nikola in the heart
and we left safe in sound.

252
00:49:34,194 --> 00:49:36,271
What did you do?

253
00:49:39,980 --> 00:49:43,628
What is it, brother? You look sad?

254
00:49:44,202 --> 00:49:45,483
Osman!

255
00:49:49,441 --> 00:49:57,154
Don't worry. It wasn't right on his heart.
He might be alive.

256
00:49:59,380 --> 00:50:02,187
Run to tell him to get well soon.

257
00:50:03,111 --> 00:50:07,266
Leave aside not listening to us,
you are going over your limit now!

258
00:50:07,404 --> 00:50:09,641
You are acting rebellious.

259
00:50:09,687 --> 00:50:16,518
I'm not doing it to be rebellious. I went there
to show them we won't leave them in peace.

260
00:50:27,241 --> 00:50:28,711
If you weren't my brother...

261
00:50:40,574 --> 00:50:44,614
Everything would be so easy,
wouldn't it, brother?

262
00:50:46,215 --> 00:50:48,907
But I'm your brother.

263
00:50:54,140 --> 00:50:58,111
Even if you don't want it,
I'll serve the Kayıs.

264
00:50:59,341 --> 00:51:03,370
Even if you don't want it,
I'll raid enemy castles every day.

265
00:51:03,449 --> 00:51:06,777
Even if you don't want it,
I'll fight every day.

266
00:51:08,708 --> 00:51:18,221
Until our tents live in prosperity and
know its enemies well.

267
00:51:29,134 --> 00:51:31,118
-Nikola.
-My dear friend.

268
00:51:48,245 --> 00:51:57,282
Come to yourselves. Victory is still ours.
We conquered Kulucahisar.

269
00:51:58,988 --> 00:52:00,547
They...

270
00:52:02,728 --> 00:52:06,974
...only saved their captives.

271
00:52:08,974 --> 00:52:15,498
What did we do?
We stabbed the Kayı tents...

272
00:52:15,760 --> 00:52:20,247
They? They stabbed me.

273
00:52:31,391 --> 00:52:33,567
Don't you ever forget that...

274
00:52:34,418 --> 00:52:40,711
...great states win wars.
Wars.

275
00:52:42,731 --> 00:52:54,270
Little ones consolidate themselves with
heroism. I don't like consolations.

276
00:52:57,146 --> 00:53:03,910
We will be on our way. Whatever the Kayıs
took from us...

277
00:53:04,680 --> 00:53:09,872
...we'll take them back one by one.

278
00:53:10,475 --> 00:53:19,585
They will come and attack us.
They will come and wound us.

279
00:53:20,438 --> 00:53:24,305
Who told you that it will be easy? Who?

280
00:53:27,162 --> 00:53:31,159
My dear friend, are there
any easy victories?

281
00:53:33,801 --> 00:53:40,577
-There is no easy victory, Nikola.
-There is no easy victory.

282
00:53:41,524 --> 00:53:46,694
Whenever you see someone successful,
know that they have been through pain.

283
00:53:48,410 --> 00:53:55,341
Then, what will we do?
We will ask for the pain.

284
00:53:56,194 --> 00:54:04,226
Then? We'll recreate Rome.
We'll be at Söğüt tomorrow.

285
00:54:05,311 --> 00:54:11,572
We'll burn it, crush it.
We'll prepare it to get occupied again.

286
00:54:11,732 --> 00:54:16,375
Let them enjoy their little heroism.

287
00:54:17,029 --> 00:54:24,567
We won't leave them a place to live,
land to stand, breath to take.

288
00:54:25,393 --> 00:54:29,051
Today, I have reborn.

289
00:54:30,305 --> 00:54:38,966
Like Mithras who killed the black bull. Like
the god of the kings, Dionysus, I've reborn.

290
00:55:01,604 --> 00:55:13,289
Who can kill someone who reborn?
Who can beat someone who reborn?

291
00:55:19,869 --> 00:55:25,070
I'm immortal now! Immortal!

292
00:55:25,070 --> 00:55:34,619
Long live, Nikola! Long live, Nikola!
Long live, Nikola! Long live, Nikola!

293
00:56:14,439 --> 00:56:16,795
With the name of Allah.

294
00:56:33,473 --> 00:56:35,753
O' people!

295
00:56:46,063 --> 00:56:49,354
The Kayı Tribe has a new Alp!

296
00:56:52,816 --> 00:56:56,911
His name is Kayı Alp.

297
00:57:15,093 --> 00:57:20,251
His grandfather is, Dündar Bey,
Süleyman Shah's son.

298
00:57:21,894 --> 00:57:28,395
His mother is a Ghazi of Kulucahisar,
Aygül Hatun.

299
00:57:41,607 --> 00:57:48,240
He will be raised as a Kayı, and become an
honorable member of our tribe.

300
00:57:50,947 --> 00:57:56,103
My good-hearted boy.
You are the pride of this tribe.

301
00:58:20,813 --> 00:58:23,881
Aygül Hatun, come on.

302
00:58:26,950 --> 00:58:33,740
Dismount your horse and hug your father
who waits for you in longing.

303
00:59:12,511 --> 00:59:25,025
My daughter... Aygül...
My daughter...

304
00:59:39,824 --> 00:59:42,089
My girl, you are wounded.

305
00:59:42,936 --> 00:59:45,782
It's the holy war. That can happen.

306
00:59:58,538 --> 01:00:05,038
Why do you hide, my girl?
You aren't the one who should be ashamed.

307
01:00:05,418 --> 01:00:07,068
It's me.

308
01:00:07,365 --> 01:00:08,198
Me.

309
01:00:13,359 --> 01:00:22,463
Oh, my Aygül. Why did you hide my
grandchild from me? Why?

310
01:01:57,584 --> 01:02:08,330
Bala. Let's go. Whoever is happy about
my arrival can come.

311
01:02:09,555 --> 01:02:11,644
As you wish, my bey.

312
01:02:55,128 --> 01:03:01,204
This is my birthday.
Today, I've reborn.

313
01:03:03,374 --> 01:03:06,115
Who wants to give me a beautiful gift?

314
01:03:06,115 --> 01:03:07,354
We! We!
We! We!

315
01:03:07,898 --> 01:03:08,817
Who?

316
01:03:08,817 --> 01:03:10,327
We! We!
We! We!

317
01:03:10,350 --> 01:03:12,894
Who wants to burn Söğüt?

318
01:03:12,894 --> 01:03:14,264
We! We!
We! We!

319
01:03:15,059 --> 01:03:18,086
Who wants to pierce the heart of the Kayıs?

320
01:03:18,086 --> 01:03:19,296
We! We!
We! We!

321
01:03:20,731 --> 01:03:26,787
The command is yours, Flatyos.
Take the cruelest men with you...

322
01:03:26,820 --> 01:03:32,758
...and in any way, turn Söğüt
into a hell...

323
01:03:32,758 --> 01:03:36,878
...and make Osman's heart burn in it.

324
01:03:37,507 --> 01:03:43,057
Söğüt is your duty, Flatyos.
And this is mine.

325
01:03:45,719 --> 01:03:50,259
When the time comes,
I'll pierce Osman's heart with this.

326
01:03:51,624 --> 01:04:00,904
Then, I'll reborn again, again and again.

327
01:04:16,374 --> 01:04:20,374
Look, what my ancestor Farabi says...

328
01:04:21,717 --> 01:04:31,327
...a city is built around virtue and
contains neighborhood relations.

329
01:04:33,616 --> 01:04:39,176
Either they are under stone walls
or tents make no difference.

330
01:04:39,898 --> 01:04:43,498
Can a tribe built with tents, be a city?

331
01:04:43,498 --> 01:04:47,898
Why can't it? As long as minds are united.

332
01:04:50,900 --> 01:04:54,900
Why would building stone walls
be civilization?

333
01:04:55,142 --> 01:04:59,142
Civilization is the thing that is
left after a calamity.

334
01:05:00,190 --> 01:05:04,190
What is left after a great calamity,
Savcı?

335
01:05:05,141 --> 01:05:18,481
Respect, love, mercy, honor, and faith.
So, everything, Lena. Everything.

336
01:05:25,451 --> 01:05:32,438
Turkism is a great tree.
Oghuz is the biggest branch of that tree.

337
01:05:32,709 --> 01:05:36,709
And Kayı is the greenest leave of
that branch.

338
01:05:37,297 --> 01:05:41,297
We are reaching for the fruit, Lena.

339
01:05:59,601 --> 01:06:02,941
Where am I in your heart, Osman?

340
01:06:07,107 --> 01:06:11,107
Is there any care left for me after
the love of the state and people?

341
01:06:15,162 --> 01:06:26,162
Bala, the heart is an armageddon flower.
Love is its leaves reaching to Allah.

342
01:06:27,370 --> 01:06:30,620
And you are my garden.

343
01:06:38,444 --> 01:06:46,384
Bala... You are my light. The fire of
your eyes illuminates the dark.

344
01:06:47,110 --> 01:06:54,260
Your smile removes all sadness, Bala.
Are you jealous of the state and people?

345
01:06:54,679 --> 01:07:02,189
If there are no lovers, no love...
What good they can do?

346
01:07:20,885 --> 01:07:24,885
We were exiled from our home in a dawn...

347
01:07:24,951 --> 01:07:28,951
Wherever we go, we aren't local.

348
01:07:29,159 --> 01:07:33,159
We have sorrow from dark nights...

349
01:07:33,437 --> 01:07:38,517
We only have a baton, a bag and Allah.

350
01:07:39,671 --> 01:07:45,461
We only have Allah... Only Allah.

351
01:07:59,474 --> 01:08:03,474
Sorrow from every breath,
it's all yours...

352
01:08:05,150 --> 01:08:09,150
Without you, there would be no love.

353
01:08:18,855 --> 01:08:21,325
Who is this man?

354
01:08:25,177 --> 01:08:28,117
Looks like a miserable man.

355
01:09:38,932 --> 01:09:42,222
Lord Nikola changed a lot.

356
01:09:44,950 --> 01:09:47,300
He has reborn.

357
01:09:54,960 --> 01:09:58,960
I hope you are as wild as they say,
Cerkutay.

358
01:09:59,538 --> 01:10:02,878
Because we'll do horrible things with you.

359
01:10:03,046 --> 01:10:07,046
What's horrible to you is cute
to us, Flatyos.

360
01:10:11,385 --> 01:10:13,665
We'll see, Cerkutay.

361
01:10:24,605 --> 01:10:29,495
When I reached Kulucahisar, the heathen
were expecting me.

362
01:10:32,197 --> 01:10:42,157
There is a traitor in the tribe. They
found it out and sent a word.

363
01:10:50,185 --> 01:10:54,185
I'm suspicious of Targon Hatun.

364
01:10:59,617 --> 01:11:01,267
Bala.

365
01:11:01,267 --> 01:11:05,447
Keep your eye on her. Follow her every step.

366
01:11:05,746 --> 01:11:09,746
As you say, my bey. But are you sure?

367
01:11:10,991 --> 01:11:17,561
I don't have evidence. But if you
bring evidence, I'll end it.

368
01:11:18,425 --> 01:11:22,425
As you say, don't worry.

369
01:11:22,757 --> 01:11:26,757
Thank you. Thank you.

370
01:11:26,926 --> 01:11:30,926
Aunt, you sound her out.

371
01:11:32,528 --> 01:11:39,828
-My bey, may I enter?
-Come, Boran.

372
01:11:48,924 --> 01:11:52,924
My bey, we have news from Kumral Abdal.

373
01:11:53,041 --> 01:11:57,041
Flatyos is going to Söğüt with his men.

374
01:12:01,043 --> 01:12:03,253
To Söğüt?

375
01:12:07,224 --> 01:12:11,224
Inform Bamsı Bey. We should meet
at the alp tent at once.

376
01:12:14,629 --> 01:12:16,919
Tell me, Boran.

377
01:12:16,999 --> 01:12:20,999
My bey, Yavlak Arslan is in
Dündar Bey's tent.

378
01:12:27,738 --> 01:12:33,168
Osman, don't go there.
You'll fight each other.

379
01:12:34,254 --> 01:12:40,484
It will be that way. But I have no
chance. They are after something.

380
01:12:40,736 --> 01:12:44,736
I should know what's their aim,
what they are after.

381
01:12:44,736 --> 01:12:51,886
Osman, when will the peace come?

382
01:12:54,205 --> 01:12:58,205
I'm struggling for the peace of
our children, Bala.

383
01:13:00,289 --> 01:13:09,129
Our destiny is a struggle. Whatever
happens today, be strong.

384
01:13:17,594 --> 01:13:20,344
For our children.

385
01:13:27,960 --> 01:13:30,500
Children...

386
01:13:53,701 --> 01:13:58,351
He entered Kulucahisar, huh?
And he severely wounded Nikola?

387
01:14:02,672 --> 01:14:06,982
How many times will you ruin my plan?

388
01:14:07,093 --> 01:14:11,983
What plan are you talking about,
Yavlak Arslan?

389
01:14:19,692 --> 01:14:24,672
You said that you separated your way,
Osman. Why are you here now?

390
01:14:24,740 --> 01:14:28,740
You don't like the ones sitting.
Are you here to sit now?

391
01:14:29,778 --> 01:14:35,008
If you are going to plan without me,
you shouldn't come to this tribe.

392
01:14:40,754 --> 01:14:46,164
You entered the castle, Osman.
You wounded Nikola on his heart.

393
01:14:47,463 --> 01:14:49,733
He wanted that.

394
01:14:49,776 --> 01:14:54,056
You took him down but couldn't kill him.

395
01:14:56,467 --> 01:14:59,527
He was destined to live, then.

396
01:14:59,902 --> 01:15:10,372
But now he knows. That castle isn't his.
I can behead them at any time.

397
01:15:11,764 --> 01:15:15,764
Despite that, he offered peace.

398
01:15:16,510 --> 01:15:18,430
Peace?

399
01:15:20,002 --> 01:15:25,812
It would be better if that dog was dead.
We'd get what we want.

400
01:15:26,008 --> 01:15:30,368
But this matter will be on the table
during the peace talk.

401
01:15:30,877 --> 01:15:33,867
What peace? What talk?

402
01:15:35,244 --> 01:15:42,254
Osman. I need this peace. My aim isn't
becoming Nikola's brother.

403
01:15:42,438 --> 01:15:45,228
It's catching him off-guard.

404
01:15:54,226 --> 01:15:59,176
Nikola, who was raided in his castle,
whose men died...

405
01:15:59,504 --> 01:16:04,774
...instead of going mad,
he is talking about peace?

406
01:16:35,854 --> 01:16:39,854
Why would someone with that power
want to make peace?

407
01:16:49,493 --> 01:16:56,303
Take the barrel to Söğüt.
Flatyos knows what to do with them.

408
01:17:01,184 --> 01:17:08,454
Osman... Let's see what he will do
when he hears that Söğüt is afire.

409
01:17:12,522 --> 01:17:16,522
Let him run after little heroisms.

410
01:17:16,792 --> 01:17:20,792
I'll march to my real target.

411
01:17:48,661 --> 01:17:57,361
We all know that Nikola needs time. You
should know that we need that time as well.

412
01:17:57,380 --> 01:18:00,580
You don't have a single moment to wait.

413
01:18:00,580 --> 01:18:06,060
Would you believe me that they
are preparing to strike us?

414
01:18:07,811 --> 01:18:11,811
Where do you get those news now, Osman?

415
01:18:11,811 --> 01:18:14,011
It's not important where I get them.

416
01:18:14,011 --> 01:18:15,851
You should listen to what I say.

417
01:18:15,851 --> 01:18:19,851
It's enough now, Osman. You intervened
my meeting that day.

418
01:18:19,851 --> 01:18:23,361
For the favor of your father,
uncle, and brothers...

419
01:18:23,361 --> 01:18:25,481
...I didn't say a thing.

420
01:18:25,481 --> 01:18:31,071
But, if you get into my way again...
If you do something to stop the peace...

421
01:18:31,297 --> 01:18:35,297
Speak, dog! Speak!
Tell me what you will do?

422
01:18:35,297 --> 01:18:43,877
You think that they are deceiving us with
peace and we are believing like little children!

423
01:18:44,727 --> 01:18:52,597
No! Not like that! While we speak of the
peace, they won't attack Söğüt.

424
01:18:52,766 --> 01:18:58,886
While your uncle and speak
of the peace, I'll attack İnegöl.

425
01:18:59,307 --> 01:19:02,107
You are making plans, huh?

426
01:19:02,769 --> 01:19:05,809
Yes, I came here to say that.

427
01:19:05,836 --> 01:19:08,956
This is a dangerous game, Yavlak Arslan.

428
01:19:08,956 --> 01:19:13,296
You ask me and my uncle to go to the castle
of a man who is wounded in his heart.

429
01:19:13,732 --> 01:19:16,742
And also, you are planning something else.

430
01:19:16,764 --> 01:19:22,594
Don't worry, Savcı Bey.
Nikola can't risk facing me.

431
01:19:23,508 --> 01:19:30,198
He knows well that I'll destroy Kulucahisar
if he does something to you.

432
01:19:33,800 --> 01:19:43,630
You are all wrong. Today's business is Söğüt.
Kulucahisa is tomorrow. İnegöl is for the future.

433
01:19:43,721 --> 01:19:48,701
If I take İnegöl, can Nikola stay
in Kulucahisar, Osman?

434
01:19:48,811 --> 01:19:51,621
You can't take İnegöl.

435
01:19:53,343 --> 01:19:57,343
Only my brother and uncle will get hurt.

436
01:20:01,682 --> 01:20:05,682
Even when you are trying to protect, you
are going over your level, Osman.

437
01:20:06,032 --> 01:20:10,032
As you got into Kulucahisar and left,
like a wolf getting into a herd...

438
01:20:10,032 --> 01:20:14,552
...we can be lions when needed,
hit the gazelles, and leave.

439
01:20:14,789 --> 01:20:18,789
All right, brother. All right.
I have no doubt about that.

440
01:20:20,825 --> 01:20:24,825
But the dagger of the enemy
is pointing at Söğüt.

441
01:20:25,838 --> 01:20:30,698
I'm going to go to Söğüt. Yavlak can go
to İnegöl if he wants to.

442
01:20:31,575 --> 01:20:35,575
And you can run into the traps of Nikola.

443
01:20:41,613 --> 01:20:50,053
But know this, when Nikola's soldiers
ambush you, it's enough for you to...

444
01:20:50,053 --> 01:20:57,513
...roar once. Your brother will
come and rescue you again.

445
01:21:50,640 --> 01:21:54,640
The heathen enemy is completely
out of control.

446
01:21:54,733 --> 01:21:57,663
There are dark clouds near Söğüt.

447
01:22:01,060 --> 01:22:06,880
It seems that they want payback for
the dagger that pierced Nikola.

448
01:22:07,577 --> 01:22:14,177
They think that Kulucahisar's worth
is a little dagger wound.

449
01:22:16,644 --> 01:22:20,794
We aren't finished yet for them
to come for payback.

450
01:22:20,829 --> 01:22:24,829
My heart isn't cold yet.

451
01:22:34,158 --> 01:22:38,158
I promise to the soul of
my ancestor, Oghuz Khagan...

452
01:22:38,158 --> 01:22:39,828
...that my heart is isn't cold yet.

453
01:22:42,907 --> 01:22:49,472
Brothers, the day for a siege
on Kulucahisar is soon.

454
01:22:50,122 --> 01:22:55,150
Today, we'll kick the enemy our of Söğüt.

455
01:22:55,980 --> 01:22:58,468
Tomorrow, maybe closer than tomorrow...

456
01:22:58,638 --> 01:23:02,638
We'll take Kulucahisar, which belongs to
our Ghazis and martyrs.

457
01:23:02,931 --> 01:23:05,071
Allahu Akbar!

458
01:23:05,122 --> 01:23:09,122
For the Ghazis who say ''Allah Allah!''

459
01:23:09,228 --> 01:23:13,228
For the faithful martyrs!

460
01:23:14,036 --> 01:23:17,096
For the commander of Ghazis,
Süleiman Shah!

461
01:23:17,096 --> 01:23:19,326
Allahu Akbar!

462
01:23:19,326 --> 01:23:25,776
For Ertuğrul Ghazi, the valiant sultan,
who is expecting our victory!

463
01:23:25,849 --> 01:23:30,769
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!

464
01:23:30,908 --> 01:23:34,908
Don't worry. Nothing will go wrong.

465
01:23:35,585 --> 01:23:39,135
We expect your victory in İnegöl.

466
01:23:39,264 --> 01:23:46,284
From now, we will put all our
benevolence to Kulucahisar.

467
01:23:48,273 --> 01:23:52,273
Of course, Dündar Bey.
Don't doubt that.

468
01:24:03,326 --> 01:24:09,416
-Our tribe and father are under your protection.
-Don't worry, brother. You can go.

469
01:24:11,859 --> 01:24:14,419
Thank you.

470
01:24:35,307 --> 01:24:37,267
My bey.

471
01:24:39,324 --> 01:24:43,624
-Abdurrahman Ghazi?
-Yes, my bey.

472
01:24:46,081 --> 01:24:49,671
What's happening in the tribe?

473
01:24:49,671 --> 01:24:57,061
Dündar, Savcı and Gündüz are
talking to Yavlak Arslan.

474
01:24:57,823 --> 01:25:02,233
-Yavlak Arslan?
-Right, my bey.

475
01:25:05,818 --> 01:25:09,818
-What about Osman?
-My bey...

476
01:25:09,823 --> 01:25:17,473
...Osman Bey is with his alps. Before the
battle, they shouted your name.

477
01:25:23,339 --> 01:25:28,109
So, he is going for
a holy war again.

478
01:25:31,441 --> 01:25:35,441
So, he is shouting my name...

479
01:25:36,328 --> 01:25:40,328
Osman Bey is just like you, my bey.

480
01:25:41,339 --> 01:25:45,339
Just like your youth, my bey.

481
01:25:47,865 --> 01:25:51,255
May Osman live long.

482
01:25:52,793 --> 01:25:59,193
May he become a bey...

483
01:26:00,311 --> 01:26:04,311
...and his name gets shouted.

484
01:26:05,763 --> 01:26:09,393
Amin, my bey.
Amin.

485
01:26:15,889 --> 01:26:19,349
-More power to your elbow.
-Thank you.

486
01:26:28,346 --> 01:26:31,826
-Was she always like this?
-She wasn't.

487
01:26:34,919 --> 01:26:38,449
She had been married to a man she didn't
love. And she turned into this.

488
01:26:38,449 --> 01:26:41,719
Did Selcan Hatun turn her into this?

489
01:26:44,259 --> 01:26:47,779
Isn't Selcan Hatun the most
powerful woman of these tents?

490
01:26:50,227 --> 01:26:55,237
Because of her age, everyone
respects her. But...

491
01:26:55,237 --> 01:26:58,537
...this is more about the mind
than the age.

492
01:27:09,357 --> 01:27:16,707
Mashallah, my girls. What
were you talking about here?

493
01:27:18,164 --> 01:27:22,574
We were talking about Aygül Hatun.
We are sad about her condition.

494
01:27:22,881 --> 01:27:28,901
-What's wrong with Aygül?
-She is a valiant warrior. A pride.

495
01:27:29,004 --> 01:27:38,564
Yes, she is. So are you. You are a bey's
daughter. We heard about his valor.

496
01:27:38,788 --> 01:27:42,788
And how they took his life, too.

497
01:27:42,888 --> 01:27:48,184
-Why did those heathens take you captive?
-I come after my father, Selcan Hatun.

498
01:27:48,184 --> 01:27:51,854
They knew what would happen
to them, if they hadn't taken me captive.

499
01:27:51,854 --> 01:27:55,434
Right, right...

500
01:27:55,853 --> 01:28:00,473
But if you are such an important woman....

501
01:28:00,473 --> 01:28:09,973
...why don't your kin nor Nikola are
looking for you? Targon, what is this?

502
01:28:10,144 --> 01:28:12,514
Tell me.

503
01:28:38,123 --> 01:28:41,213
-Selcan Hatun.
-Yes.

504
01:28:41,213 --> 01:28:44,193
-Aygül is in Dündar Bey's tent.
-So?

505
01:28:44,193 --> 01:28:47,553
Hazal Hatun just entered the tent.

506
01:29:01,906 --> 01:29:05,906
Did you put your eyes on the
Bey's place, Aygül?

507
01:29:08,111 --> 01:29:11,601
I put my eyes on you, Hazal.

508
01:29:13,352 --> 01:29:16,502
I put my eyes on my mother's killer.

509
01:29:27,588 --> 01:29:40,068
Don't you remember that your mother
attempted to kill all Kayı Beys and women?

510
01:29:43,356 --> 01:29:49,436
I had a score to settle with you.
I remember that.

511
01:30:08,346 --> 01:30:11,786
Where did you find that sword, Lena?

512
01:30:14,673 --> 01:30:17,703
It looks good on your hand.

513
01:30:23,164 --> 01:30:27,029
If there is a lunatic in the tribe who
is wandering with a sword...

514
01:30:27,029 --> 01:30:29,539
...you should take a measure, Aygül.

515
01:30:30,884 --> 01:30:34,884
What good can you do even if you
had measures from up and down, Lena?

516
01:30:41,743 --> 01:30:45,133
Be careful, Aygül.

517
01:30:46,299 --> 01:30:49,449
I'm not your step mother.

518
01:30:51,274 --> 01:30:54,634
I have no pity.

519
01:31:18,457 --> 01:31:21,987
Come on, hurry.
I need to catch with my uncle.

520
01:31:24,116 --> 01:31:26,196
Savcı Bey!

521
01:31:27,603 --> 01:31:32,833
There are sounds coming from Dündar Bey's
tent. Lena Hatun and Aygül Hatun are fighting.

522
01:31:32,899 --> 01:31:34,909
What?

523
01:31:47,269 --> 01:31:49,789
Take this, Rum girl!

524
01:31:54,577 --> 01:31:57,827
Come, then, Alişar's wife!

525
01:32:21,094 --> 01:32:23,204
Aygül!

526
01:32:28,525 --> 01:32:31,935
-Aygül...
-Don't move, Savcı bey!

527
01:32:33,087 --> 01:32:38,337
Aren't you an alp of Osman bey?

528
01:32:43,588 --> 01:32:47,588
What are you doing here while your
bey is on a campaign?

529
01:32:47,897 --> 01:32:50,947
So, Osman bey went to Söğüt?

530
01:32:52,444 --> 01:32:55,874
I have no quarrel with you, Savcı Bey.

531
01:33:13,119 --> 01:33:17,119
But this isn't the end of it.

532
01:33:27,376 --> 01:33:31,376
-Are you all right?
-Savcı bey!

533
01:33:31,857 --> 01:33:38,627
If this woman doesn't leave the tents,
either I, Hazal Hatun or she will die!

534
01:34:41,607 --> 01:34:45,377
Hold there. What's in them?

535
01:34:45,602 --> 01:34:49,802
-It's from Gemlik. Olive oil.
-Give me.

536
01:35:00,463 --> 01:35:02,303
Here.

537
01:35:10,202 --> 01:35:13,592
-It's fine, go on.
-Thank you.

538
01:35:54,002 --> 01:35:56,912
Here we go, Cerkutay.

539
01:35:57,948 --> 01:36:00,978
Everyone to their positions.

540
01:36:35,653 --> 01:36:39,653
-So, we separate here?
-True, Bamsı Bey.

541
01:36:39,653 --> 01:36:42,853
When we find out the goal of the
weasels, we'll let each other know.

542
01:36:42,853 --> 01:36:46,983
-Once we find out theirs, ours will be decided.
-All right, my lion. All right.

543
01:36:46,983 --> 01:36:51,183
-Godspeed!
-Thank you. May Allah bless our efforts.

544
01:36:52,197 --> 01:36:54,137
Come on!

545
01:37:10,735 --> 01:37:20,135
We are the warriors of Kayı!
Our intentions are for Allah's approval.

546
01:37:20,135 --> 01:37:28,355
We came to these lands to spread
the religion of Allah, the true faith!

547
01:37:28,355 --> 01:37:37,995
Thank Allah for protecting us against
tyrants, who puts faith in our hearts!

548
01:37:37,995 --> 01:37:45,995
Forever, for justice!
Forever, for freedom! Allahu Akbar!

549
01:37:55,313 --> 01:38:04,653
We don't want you here! Get out!
Leave here! We don't want you!

550
01:38:04,967 --> 01:38:12,987
You filthy barbarians! Get out!
Nobody wants you here, you barbarians!

551
01:38:25,641 --> 01:38:29,641
Osman bey is on his way to Söğüt.

552
01:38:42,166 --> 01:38:44,936
-Attack me!
-Attack you?

553
01:38:44,936 --> 01:38:47,806
I told you to do it!

554
01:38:57,994 --> 01:39:01,274
Targon Hatun, what's going on here?

555
01:39:03,586 --> 01:39:09,106
I'm talking to you, Targon! What are
you doing here? Who is this man?

556
01:39:15,226 --> 01:39:20,543
'Osman left the tents. He is on his way
to Söğüt' What does that mean?

557
01:39:21,113 --> 01:39:27,418
It means that there is a traitor in the
tents. Someone is leaking information.

558
01:39:30,113 --> 01:39:34,943
-What were you doing here?
-I'm not used to sitting, Bala Hatun.

559
01:39:35,039 --> 01:39:40,859
I wanted to take a walk. Then, I saw
this man. I realized he was after something.

560
01:39:46,102 --> 01:39:51,682
Don't get far again without telling
anyone. You are under our protection.

561
01:39:51,682 --> 01:39:55,682
As it's known, one who leaves the tents
becomes prey for the wolves.

562
01:39:59,700 --> 01:40:01,370
Let's go back to the tribe.

563
01:40:02,433 --> 01:40:03,993
Come on.

564
01:40:41,279 --> 01:40:43,989
What does that mean, Nicola?

565
01:40:45,901 --> 01:40:49,591
This means the castle has been civilized.

566
01:40:50,647 --> 01:40:55,531
Savcı Bey, should I have brought rugs,
carpets or sheepskin?

567
01:40:55,531 --> 01:40:58,531
Stop talking no sense about civilization!

568
01:40:58,648 --> 01:41:05,208
- We don't appreciate this insult!
- Get off your throne, talk face to face.

569
01:41:05,559 --> 01:41:08,519
I was hoping that we'd make peace.

570
01:41:15,546 --> 01:41:18,243
You can't make peace like that.

571
01:41:18,243 --> 01:41:22,213
Hah, this is so a Turkish Bey move.

572
01:41:27,825 --> 01:41:32,805
What do you think Turks Beys are, Nicola?

573
01:41:33,734 --> 01:41:35,064
Ha?

574
01:41:35,072 --> 01:41:39,782
We have made thousands of wars
and peace with...

575
01:41:39,869 --> 01:41:44,189
those Chinese Emperors who you couldn't
even imagine in your dreams...

576
01:41:44,412 --> 01:41:49,702
and those Caesers who you are proud of.

577
01:41:55,750 --> 01:41:59,991
I love Turks, Savcı Bey.
I really do.

578
01:41:59,991 --> 01:42:05,061
You claim all the great empires
in history. That's cool.

579
01:42:05,477 --> 01:42:12,487
Beys. Kayı Beys.
You are talking to Rome Governor.

580
01:42:25,868 --> 01:42:29,358
Kayı Beys, ha?
Kayı Beys.

581
01:42:31,031 --> 01:42:34,581
Do you know the story of Oghuzs, Nicola?

582
01:42:36,538 --> 01:42:40,688
I like history, Dündar Bey.
I know but...

583
01:42:41,597 --> 01:42:46,927
You should remember that all the history
was written in Rome.

584
01:42:47,021 --> 01:42:54,736
You live like moles in nooks.
You capture women, olds an kids.

585
01:42:54,736 --> 01:42:57,396
And you call it your history.

586
01:43:00,097 --> 01:43:04,527
Turkish is spoken from Chinese to Rome
borders.

587
01:43:04,611 --> 01:43:09,701
Do you know why Nicola?
Because our ancestors conquered there.

588
01:43:11,346 --> 01:43:15,196
We even conquered this castle you are
living in, Nicola.

589
01:43:15,833 --> 01:43:18,093
Do you want it back?

590
01:43:29,573 --> 01:43:32,673
Do you want war?

591
01:43:45,817 --> 01:43:48,227
Do you want war?!

592
01:44:26,303 --> 01:44:29,043
We need fire.

593
01:44:39,299 --> 01:44:44,069
Turks are friendly.
They will give me.

594
01:44:48,838 --> 01:44:54,188
Firstly, you'll accept that Kulucahisar...

595
01:44:54,305 --> 01:44:59,115
is under my command.

596
01:45:02,284 --> 01:45:06,930
Secondly, you are going to swear on...

597
01:45:06,930 --> 01:45:12,550
your dignity and honor that you
are not going to attack Kulucahisar.

598
01:45:18,412 --> 01:45:22,402
What?
How else can I be sure?

599
01:45:23,211 --> 01:45:25,804
This agreement won't work.

600
01:45:25,804 --> 01:45:32,644
Savcı Bey, there would not be an agreement
without this article.

601
01:45:33,087 --> 01:45:37,107
What's the point of making an agreement...

602
01:45:37,261 --> 01:45:39,881
if you are going to attack here anytime
you want?

603
01:45:44,045 --> 01:45:45,665
And...

604
01:45:46,946 --> 01:45:48,266
Osman...

605
01:45:50,970 --> 01:45:53,410
he is not going to come here again.

606
01:45:53,986 --> 01:45:56,596
Neither in daylight nor in night.

607
01:45:57,143 --> 01:46:03,113
Neither through the door nor
through the gates.

608
01:46:04,676 --> 01:46:06,536
Do you understand me?

609
01:46:13,387 --> 01:46:17,667
What's it? Are you worried about the
fact that you can't hold Osman down?

610
01:46:17,758 --> 01:46:21,988
- It's our concern, Nicola.
- No, that's not true.

611
01:46:22,694 --> 01:46:28,124
This is all Rome's and Turks' concern,
Savcı Bey.

612
01:46:29,016 --> 01:46:32,396
Osman is a rebel.

613
01:46:34,643 --> 01:46:39,983
Look here, Rome Governor!
Watch your mouth about my brother.

614
01:46:40,125 --> 01:46:43,135
Even in front of me, how you dare!

615
01:46:44,015 --> 01:46:45,235
Okay.

616
01:46:46,490 --> 01:46:50,300
I didn't know you loved Osman that much.

617
01:47:00,120 --> 01:47:04,990
Let's cut it short.

618
01:47:05,073 --> 01:47:09,573
This article must be added
to the agreement.

619
01:47:12,747 --> 01:47:18,307
If Rome attack any property of Turks...

620
01:47:18,935 --> 01:47:22,965
this agreement will be broken.

621
01:47:23,696 --> 01:47:26,026
Turkish property?

622
01:47:29,381 --> 01:47:33,291
What does this mean?
This is a broad term.

623
01:47:55,387 --> 01:47:59,387
What is this, Nicola?!

624
01:48:48,070 --> 01:48:49,830
Hi, blacksmith.

625
01:48:50,788 --> 01:48:52,698
Tell me.

626
01:48:53,877 --> 01:48:55,767
I need fire.

627
01:49:00,273 --> 01:49:03,103
Do you, really?

628
01:49:05,982 --> 01:49:07,792
Osman!

629
01:49:46,258 --> 01:49:48,478
Sogut is my town!

630
01:49:49,253 --> 01:49:54,103
You have to ask my permission
before visiting here.

631
01:49:54,109 --> 01:49:57,039
I am just like you, showing up
without permission, Osman.

632
01:49:57,039 --> 01:50:01,769
You are a guest.
The first move is yours, then.

633
01:50:03,833 --> 01:50:05,643
Sure.

634
01:51:15,443 --> 01:51:17,143
Have a nice day.

635
01:51:33,763 --> 01:51:39,403
Hey! What are you doing with that
barrel? You ruined the ground!

636
01:51:45,036 --> 01:51:47,566
I'll clean it with fire.

637
01:51:58,132 --> 01:52:03,032
Hey! Where are you going?
Give the candle back to me!

638
01:52:03,431 --> 01:52:05,166
I'm talking to you!

639
01:52:05,166 --> 01:52:07,206
Bring the candle back!

640
01:52:11,809 --> 01:52:15,669
I told you I'd clean up.

641
01:52:48,496 --> 01:52:51,126
I missed you, Bamsı.

642
01:53:26,978 --> 01:53:29,998
You took me and left in the castle
last time, Osman.

643
01:53:30,658 --> 01:53:34,408
So, who is going to save your
capture brother and uncle?

644
01:53:35,422 --> 01:53:37,382
Dogs!

645
01:53:38,611 --> 01:53:42,441
I left the castle with you, I saved
my men.

646
01:53:42,441 --> 01:53:46,601
Now I'll arrive at the castle with you,
and save my brother and uncle.

647
01:53:49,735 --> 01:53:52,195
- My Bey, my Bey!
- Do it!

648
01:53:52,195 --> 01:53:53,665
No!

649
01:54:01,780 --> 01:54:06,850
Osman Bey.
You can lean on me from now on.

650
01:54:07,284 --> 01:54:09,574
Thank you, my valiant.

651
01:54:10,139 --> 01:54:13,789
- Tell me your name.
- My name is Gence Bey.

652
01:54:57,402 --> 01:54:59,042
Nice.

653
01:55:03,182 --> 01:55:05,552
Just like that.

654
01:55:06,618 --> 01:55:08,578
Just like that.

655
01:55:31,880 --> 01:55:36,428
You are looking far better now!

656
01:55:36,428 --> 01:55:41,898
We just need some... yeah
now it is fantastic.

657
01:55:42,032 --> 01:55:45,922
It's absolutely fantastic!

658
01:55:59,069 --> 01:56:01,999
You ignoble dog!

659
01:56:03,683 --> 01:56:06,153
You are going to pay!

660
01:56:06,575 --> 01:56:10,105
You are going to pay for this!

661
01:56:10,986 --> 01:56:12,686
Here we are.

662
01:56:26,728 --> 01:56:30,288
It's excellent!

663
01:56:40,899 --> 01:56:45,529
I asked Osman.
"How are you going to get out of here?"

664
01:56:45,916 --> 01:56:49,274
Do you wonder his respond?

665
01:56:49,274 --> 01:56:55,484
"I am going to leave like a wolf
that leaves from a sheepfold."

666
01:56:56,110 --> 01:56:58,600
Hold on, uncle!

667
01:56:58,656 --> 01:57:01,836
We... we... we are going to kill you!

668
01:57:09,561 --> 01:57:13,631
- Dündar Bey, he did what he said.
- I'll kill you.

669
01:57:13,631 --> 01:57:16,987
- Dündar Bey, you are so handsome now.
- I'll kill you!

670
01:57:16,987 --> 01:57:19,027
I'll murder you!

671
01:57:23,346 --> 01:57:26,176
Hold on, uncle, hold on.

672
01:57:26,246 --> 01:57:30,568
Dündar Bey, believe me.
It's going to be okay.

673
01:57:30,568 --> 01:57:32,558
You ignoble dog!

674
01:57:33,077 --> 01:57:35,297
You are going to pay.

675
01:57:35,346 --> 01:57:38,024
You are going... to... pay

676
01:57:38,024 --> 01:57:41,374
Hold on, uncle!
Hold on!

677
01:57:43,601 --> 01:57:46,471
Uncle... uncle!

678
01:57:47,322 --> 01:57:51,862
Hello! I am the new uncle!
Hahaha!

679
01:57:52,216 --> 01:57:56,126
You look fantastic!
Give me a minute, here, here...

680
01:57:56,618 --> 01:58:01,418
Hold on for a second!
Yeah here it is!

681
01:58:04,058 --> 01:58:06,598
I need to squish it a little bit.

682
01:58:07,814 --> 01:58:11,094
Yes, it's getting better.

683
01:58:11,108 --> 01:58:15,698
Let's press here too.
Beautiful

684
01:58:15,755 --> 01:58:19,915
And here is some more just for you!

685
01:58:23,090 --> 01:58:28,680
I love sculpturing!
Believe me, you look better now

686
01:58:29,505 --> 01:58:31,705
Yes.

687
01:58:34,320 --> 01:58:38,440
- I should leave, Osman Bey.
- Be my guest, come to my tent.

688
01:58:39,645 --> 01:58:41,845
You are too busy.

689
01:58:46,208 --> 01:58:50,478
- I'll come someday.
- Eyvallah(thank you) I look forward for it.

690
01:59:11,561 --> 01:59:15,031
He says my uncle and my brother
are in Kulucahisar.

691
01:59:20,388 --> 01:59:22,568
Where is Bamsı Bey?

692
01:59:41,651 --> 01:59:45,161
My Osman, my Osman.
Check this out.

693
01:59:45,435 --> 01:59:48,285
- Look.
- Masha Allah(praise be!)

694
01:59:48,450 --> 01:59:51,320
Look who I run across with on my way here.

695
01:59:53,422 --> 01:59:55,412
Cerkutay.

696
02:00:09,079 --> 02:00:12,823
Bamsı Bey.
We are done with Sogut.

697
02:00:12,823 --> 02:00:16,753
Why, son?
It's Nicola again, isn't it?

698
02:00:17,405 --> 02:00:20,105
Yes, actually.

699
02:00:22,955 --> 02:00:26,775
- Son, what are you going to do?
- I'll go to Kulucahisar.

700
02:00:35,889 --> 02:00:37,999
What's it, Vladius?

701
02:00:38,955 --> 02:00:41,765
Are you bored of me?

702
02:00:43,365 --> 02:00:44,915
Ha?

703
02:00:47,163 --> 02:00:52,013
I told you.
I'll visit that castle more often.

704
02:00:55,280 --> 02:00:58,520
Until you leave there!

705
02:01:18,664 --> 02:01:25,073
You are wrong! We need to deal with
Sogut first, then Kulucahisar, then Inegol.

706
02:01:25,493 --> 02:01:31,703
What if I conquer Inegol? Can Nicola
manage Kulucahisar then?

707
02:01:32,045 --> 02:01:35,065
You can't take Inegol.

708
02:01:35,658 --> 02:01:39,261
My uncle and my brother will be victims!

709
02:01:39,261 --> 02:01:41,874
You are crossing the respect
line, Osman!

710
02:01:41,874 --> 02:01:47,854
You can leave Kulucahisar like a wolf
leaving from a sheepfold, but I am the lion.

711
02:01:48,273 --> 02:01:50,313
I kill the whole gazelle herd.

712
02:01:50,313 --> 02:01:54,933
I'll go to Sogut. Yavlak can go
to Inegol.

713
02:01:55,878 --> 02:01:58,788
And Nicola will entrap you!

714
02:02:00,286 --> 02:02:04,306
Osman, Osman is right again.

715
02:02:08,160 --> 02:02:12,340
He tricked us, ignoble.

716
02:02:14,941 --> 02:02:18,571
That dog planned this all.

717
02:02:23,917 --> 02:02:27,727
But it's not going to be that easy, uncle.

718
02:02:27,869 --> 02:02:31,569
I am going to kill him before he kills me.

719
02:02:31,569 --> 02:02:35,449
We don't fear anyone, son.

720
02:03:14,061 --> 02:03:17,261
Talking about how glorious Turks are all
the time...

721
02:03:44,895 --> 02:03:50,395
Dear Kayı Beys. Do you know what
I should do now?

722
02:03:51,998 --> 02:03:56,758
I should wait for you to hear the
news from Sogut being destroyed.

723
02:04:01,239 --> 02:04:03,769
But I won't be able to wait, I guess.

724
02:04:42,176 --> 02:04:43,886
Father.

725
02:04:52,683 --> 02:04:54,753
- Gündüz.
- Father.

726
02:04:58,111 --> 02:04:59,861
Son.

727
02:05:11,225 --> 02:05:14,605
I have a bad feeling, Abdurrahman Ghazi.

728
02:05:47,337 --> 02:05:49,927
Our men are returning!

729
02:05:55,972 --> 02:06:00,222
Vladius is wounded!
He is wounded!

730
02:06:00,869 --> 02:06:03,759
Open the gates!
Gates!

731
02:06:19,927 --> 02:06:24,817
When Nicola entraps you,
just scream for help.

732
02:06:24,817 --> 02:06:29,677
I will save you no matter what!

733
02:07:44,365 --> 02:07:47,885
Vladius, vladius, my saint friend!

734
02:07:47,924 --> 02:07:50,504
Vladius, Vladius!

